d": "step_13", "tool": "edges_between", "args": {"u": 547, "v": 641, "window": [39251, 77651]}, "result_digest": "2d02f8d3c77f5c35", "result_summary": "{\"connected\": false, \"n_events_u_to_v\": 0, \"n_events_v_to_u\": 0, \"u\": 547, \"v\": 641, \"window\": [39251, 77651]}", "latency_ms": 0, "tokens_before": 39124, "tokens_after": 39124, "ok": true, "error": ""}, {"step_id": "step_14", "tool": "neighbors", "args": {"node": 547, "window": [39251, 77651], "direction": "out"}, "result_digest": "c9487570ce0ee643", "result_summary": "{\"direction\": \"out\", \"n_neighbors\": 67, \"neighbors\": [10, 15, 50, 64, 91, 104, 150, 153, 203, 204, 229, 239, 281, 348, 407, 453, 482, 518, 534, 562, 585, 599, 733, 742, 776, 831, 873, 874, 879, 889, 924, 977, 1014, 1036, 1094, 1108, 1135, 1198, 1200, 1211, 1216, 1220, 1232, 1239, 1240, 1288, 1340, 1346, 1377, 1418, 1458, 1504, 1530, 1558, 1581, 1619, 1642, 1781, 1824, 1839, 1893, 1897, 1904, 1980, 1982, 1992, 1993], \"node\": 547, \"window\": [39251, 77651]}", "latency_ms": 2, "tokens_before": 39124, "tokens_after": 39124, "ok": true, "error": ""}], "final_claim": {"task_id": "t_b1e97ee9", "decision": "absent", "mechanism": "cascade", "entities": [547, 641], "window": [39251, 77651], "confidence": 0.93, "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "No time-respecting cascade from 547 to 641 exists in [39251, 77651]. Under the \u0394\u2264600 constraint, 547 reaches 74 nodes and 641 is not among them (step_01), with zero enumerated paths (step_06). Critically, removing the waiting-time limit entirely still fails: 547 reaches 548 nodes but never 641 (step_03), showing the obstruction is temporal ordering rather than a too-strict delay budget. The timeseries explain why: 547's activity accelerates late (1 to 26 events per bin) while 641's decays to zero and ceases after t=68050 (steps 07, 08), so the two nodes' active periods are essentially anti-aligned and influence would need to travel backwards in time; restricting to the earlier window where 641 was still active also yields no path (step_11). Confounders were tested and rejected: the window is event-dense (8952 events, step_02) and both nodes are hubs with ~70 interactions each (step_04), so neither volume nor popularity produces a cascade; the surrounding static structure is large and richly connected (step_05), yet there is no direct 547-641 edge (step_13) and 547's out-neighbors are disjoint from 641's in-neighbors (steps 14, 09), leaving no relay; coarse-bin co-activity is misleadingly high (Jaccard 0.75, step_12) but reflects shared bins rather than valid ordering; and the reverse direction fails as well (step_10)."}, "raw_final_response": "All evidence gathered. Let me summarize the findings.\n\n**Key findings:**\n\n1. **No 600-unit cascade exists** (step_01): 547 reaches 74 nodes under the \u0394\u2264600 constraint, but 641 is not among them. No paths enumerated (step_06).\n\n2. **Not even an unconstrained temporal path exists** (step_03): relaxing max_wait entirely, 547 reaches 548 nodes \u2014 still not 641. The failure is not about the 600-unit budget being too tight; the temporal order itself forbids it.\n\n3. **Mechanism \u2014 anti-aligned activity timing** (steps 07, 08): 547's activity *ramps up* late (1\u21921\u21922\u21923\u21927\u219213\u219217\u219226 across bins), while 641's activity *decays to zero* early (37\u219215\u21927\u21926\u21921\u21922\u21920\u21920). 641 is completely silent after t\u224868050, precisely when 547 becomes most active. Influence would have to travel backwards in time.\n\n4. **Confounders ruled out:**\n   - *Volume*: 8,952 events over 1,977 nodes (step_02) \u2014 a dense graph that nonetheless yields no path.\n   - *Popularity*: both nodes are well-connected hubs, 70 and 68 events respectively (step_04) \u2014 high degree alone produces no cascade.\n   - *Static connectivity*: the 2-hop neighborhood is large and richly connected (step_05), yet 547's 67 out-neighbors (step_14) and 641's 66 in-neighbors (step_09) are **disjoint** \u2014 no 2-hop relay \u2014 and there is no direct edge (step_13).\n   - *Co-activity*: coarse-binned co-activity is deceptively high (Jaccard 0.75, step_12), a classic false positive; bin-level overlap hides the within-window ordering that actually blocks transmission.\n   - *Direction/sub-window*: reverse direction also fails (step_10), and restricting to the earlier window where 641 was alive also fails (step_11).\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_b1e97ee9\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [547, 641],\n  \"window\": [39251, 77651],\n  \"confidence\": 0.93,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"No time-respecting cascade from 547 to 641 exists in [39251, 77651]. Under the \u0394\u2264600 constraint, 547 reaches 74 nodes and 641 is not among them (step_01), with zero enumerated paths (step_06). Critically, removing the waiting-time limit entirely still fails: 547 reaches 548 nodes but never 641 (step_03), showing the obstruction is temporal ordering rather than a too-strict delay budget. The timeseries explain why: 547's activity accelerates late (1 to 26 events per bin) while 641's decays to zero and ceases after t=68050 (steps 07, 08), so the two nodes' active periods are essentially anti-aligned and influence would need to travel backwards in time; restricting to the earlier window where 641 was still active also yields no path (step_11). Confounders were tested and rejected: the window is event-dense (8952 events, step_02) and both nodes are hubs with ~70 interactions each (step_04), so neither volume nor popularity produces a cascade; the surrounding static structure is large and richly connected (step_05), yet there is no direct 547-641 edge (step_13) and 547's out-neighbors are disjoint from 641's in-neighbors (steps 14, 09), leaving no relay; coarse-bin co-activity is misleadingly high (Jaccard 0.75, step_12) but reflects shared bins rather than valid ordering; and the reverse direction fails as well (step_10).\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 49198, "total_output_tokens": 4332, "total_tokens": 53530, "total_latency_ms": 56460, "llm_calls": 7, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}